      "function_role": "omission-policy-4th-avoidance",
      "narrative": "The 4th scale degree on dominant 7th chords carries strong tension and must not be used as a phrase-ending note. Chapter 2 p.6 states: 'The 4th tone of major and dominant 7th chord/scales contains much tension and thus usually isn't emphasized. The 4th is usually treated as a passing tone between the 3rd and 5th scale tones. When in major or dominant keys don't end a phrase on the 4th.'",
