      "function_role": "color-tone-pretty-notes",
      "narrative": "The preferred color tones that give the dominant 7th chord its characteristic brightness and interest are the 6th, major 7th, 9th, and raised 4th. Chapter 7 p.25 states: 'The pretty notes for major and dominant 7th chords/scales are the 6, 7, 9, and #4.'",
