    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-bebop-scale",
      "narrative": "The bebop dominant scale adds a chromatic passing tone (major 7th / B natural on C7) to the standard Mixolydian scale to create an 8-note pattern that aligns chord tones to strong beats. Chapter 8 p.28 defines it: 'The bebop scale contains one added tone to each of the four most used scales. Dominant 7th, C7 = C D E F G A Bb B C (The underlined tone is the added tone.)' Chapter 16 p.54 reinforces: 'BEBOP = C7 = C D E F G A Bb B C.'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
      "references": [
        {
