    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "rhythmic-placement-bebop-added-tone-upbeat",
      "narrative": "The added chromatic tone (B natural) in the dominant bebop scale must never fall on a downbeat. Chapter 8 p.28 is explicit: 'Don't allow the B natural (added tone) to fall on a downbeat. The added tone must always come on the upbeat in order to give it the jazz sound we are used to hearing.' Chapter 16 p.54 echoes: 'Play B natural as a passing tone. It should always appear on an upbeat, never on the downbeat.'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
