    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "substitution-bebop-ii-chord-bridge",
      "narrative": "The dominant bebop scale can function as a substitute for the minor ii chord in a ii-V progression, allowing one scale to cover both chords. Chapter 8 p.28 states: 'The dom.7th bebop scale can act as a substitute for the minor ii chord. Example: C7 bebop scale (C D E F G A Bb B C) could also be played over the G- chord and vice versa. The chords are interchangeable over the scale.'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
