    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "voice-leading-guide-tone-targeting",
      "narrative": "When first learning to improvise over dominant 7th chords, target the 3rd and 7th as primary melodic destinations to internalize the harmony. Chapter 11 p.38 instructs: 'Improvise on the 3rd or 7th of each chord in order to get the sound and feel of the harmony in your mind.' Chapter 19 p.65 affirms: 'Emphasize 3rds and 7ths. They are the important notes in the dominant 7th scale/chord.'",
