    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-resolution-up-perfect-fourth",
      "narrative": "The dominant 7th chord has a natural gravitational pull toward the chord a perfect fourth above, and improvised lines should reflect this tendency. Chapter 16 p.54 states: 'Dominants typically want to resolve to a chord up a perfect 4th (C7 wants to resolve to F, F-, F7 etc.).' Altered tones on dominant chords 'usually resolve by half-step to a scale or chord tone' of the target (chapter 16 p.54).",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
