    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-7-scale-palette",
      "narrative": "Chapter 16 p.54 lays out seven distinct scale options available over a dominant 7th chord, forming a complete palette from basic to highly altered: the basic Dominant 7th (Mixolydian), Bebop, Lydian Dominant (C7#4), Whole-Tone (C7+), Diminished (C7b9), Diminished Whole-Tone (C7+9), and Spanish/Jewish scale. Aebersold prescribes experimenting with all of them over the cycle-of-dominant-7ths track: 'The proper use of these various scales is part of what makes jazz so appealing.'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
      "references": [
