    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-lydian-dominant",
      "narrative": "The Lydian Dominant scale (Mixolydian with a raised 4th) is a favored color option for dominant 7th chords. Chapter 16 p.54 specifies: 'LYDIAN DOM. = C7#4 = C D E F# G A Bb C The #4 was/is a favorite note.' The #4 also appears on the color-tone list: 'The pretty notes for major and dominant 7th chords/scales are the 6, 7, 9, and #4' (chapter 7 p.25).",
