    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-whole-tone",
      "narrative": "The whole-tone scale is a six-note symmetrical option for augmented dominant chords (C7+). Chapter 16 p.54 describes: 'WHOLE-TONE = C7+ = C D E F# G# Bb C This scale only has 6 tones. It is a symmetrical scale used often in cartoon music and by DeBussy and Ravel.' Chapter 18 p.61 notes only two whole-tone scales exist, covering C7, E7, F7, G7, A7, and B7.",
