    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "idiom-specific-spanish-jewish-scale-minor-key",
      "narrative": "When a dominant 7th chord appears in a minor-key context, the Spanish or Jewish scale (equivalent to the harmonic minor built on the 4th) provides an idiomatic color option. Chapter 16 p.54 states: 'SPANISH or JEWISH SCALE = C7(b9) = C Db E F G Ab Bb C This scale is used often when playing in a minor key. It's the same as F harmonic minor.'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
