    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-dorian-preference",
      "narrative": "Aebersold mandates the Dorian mode as the default minor scale throughout the book. Chapter 2 p.7 states: 'Every minor scale employed on the record and in the musical examples is in the Dorian mode.' Chapter 15 p.53 further ranks the order of preference: 'I have found the order of preference to be Dorian, Bebop, Melodic, Blues, Pentatonic, and then any of the remaining Minor scale choices,' placing Dorian first and pure minor last.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "vol-1-how-to-play-jazz-and-improvise",
