      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-dorian-major-relationship",
      "narrative": "Understanding the Dorian mode through its relationship to the major scale aids internalization and allows reuse of known fingerings. Chapter 2 p.7 explains: 'The minor scale (dorian) is really the same as a major scale whose root lies a whole step below the root of the dorian minor. Example: F- is the same as Eb major (3 flats).'",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
