      "function_role": "idiom-specific-blues-scale-static-minor",
      "narrative": "The blues scale may be used over a minor 7th chord when that chord is sustained for two or more measures, providing a soulful alternative to the Dorian mode. Chapter 12 p.41 states: 'The blues scale can also be used over minor chords when the minor chord is sounded for 2, 4, 8, or 16 measures or longer.'",
