    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "idiom-specific-dorian-blues-alternation",
      "narrative": "For extended minor sections, alternating between Dorian and the blues scale (both sharing the same root) is the recommended strategy for maintaining musical variety. Chapter 12 p.41 advises: 'When playing in minor tonalities you may choose to alternate between the dorian minor and the blues scale, both having the same root tone.'",
